Master-Slave Architecture:
--------------------------
    Master (controller)
    Slave (Agents/Nodes)

    why:
    ----
    improve performance
    run multiple jobs efficiently
    distribute workload

    problem without slaves:
    -----------------------
    100 jobs --> all run on master
    slower execution

    solution:
    ---------
    distribute jobs:
        slave1 --> 20 jobs
        slave2 --> 20 jobs
        slave3 --> 20 jobs
        slave4 --> 20 jobs
        slave5 --> 20 jobs
        etc

    Key Concepts:
    -------------
    Master Responsibilities:
        - stores job configurations
        - manages builds
        - schedules jobs
    Location:
        JENKINS_HOME/jobs

    Slave Responsibilities:
    -----------------------
        - executes jobs
        - downloads code
        - runs build

    Important Points:
    ----------------
        - jenkins NOT installed on slave
        - Only java required
        Uses agent.jar to connect

    Where Code is Stored:
    ---------------------
    Job config --> master
    source code --> slave




















